/P 809 0 R
/E (In this Arduino program, a push button is connected to pin 5 \(BUTTON_PIN\) and a TM1637 4-digit display is connected to pins 8 \(CLK\) and 9 \(DIO\). The TM1637Display library is used to control the display.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
381 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 810 0 R
/E (The setup\(\) function runs once when the Arduino starts. It sets the button pin as INPUT, sets the display brightness using setBrightness\(\), and displays 0 initially.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
382 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 811 0 R
/E (The loop\(\) function runs continuously. It reads the current button state using digitalRead\(\) and compares it with the previous state stored in lastButtonState.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
383 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 812 0 R
/E (When the button is pressed \(change from LOW to HIGH\), the count value increases by 1. The updated count is shown on the display using showNumberDec\(\). If the count goes above 9999, it resets back to 0.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
384 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 813 0 R
/E (A small delay\(\) is used to prevent multiple counts from a single press.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
